== MU10: the staff, and the maqam ladder ==

-- Scene 1: where a note sits is its pitch --
   C4 E4 F5 A5 on the treble staff: steps -2 0 8 10 (0 is the bottom line, 8 the top)
  [ok]   C4 sits on the first ledger line below the treble staff, E4 on its bottom line, F5 on its top line, A5 on the first ledger above
  [ok]   and exactly two ledger lines are drawn: one under C4, one over A5
  [ok]   stems go UP below the middle line and DOWN above it
  [ok]   a low voice gets the BASS clef, where G2 is the bottom line, A3 the top, and middle C the first ledger above

-- Scene 2: the length is the shape --
   beams: 2 (2 3 notes; levels 1 2 )
  [ok]   two eighths on a beat are BEAMED; two sixteenths and an eighth on the next beat take a second beam
  [ok]   an eighth alone on its beat takes a FLAG instead
  [ok]   a dotted quarter is drawn with its dot
   C5 for six beats from beat 4: 3 heads, 1 tie(s)
  [ok]   a note that crosses a barline is written as two notes TIED: a whole note into a half
  [ok]   a half note begun on the fourth beat is a quarter in its bar, tied to a quarter in the next
   rests: 4 16 (sixteenths)
  [ok]   every gap is a rest, and an empty bar is ONE whole rest

-- Scene 3: accidentals hold to the barline; the quarter tones are written --
   C#5 C#5 C5 E-half-flat | C5 E-half-flat: accidentals shown 1 0 -0.500 -0.500
  [ok]   the sharp is written once, the natural cancels it, and the next bar needs none: # - n
  [ok]   the half-flat is written in BOTH bars -- the barline forgets it
  [ok]   and is drawn as Arabic notation draws it: a flat with a stroke through it

-- Scene 4: chords, voices and pages --
  [ok]   a second inside a chord sets its two heads either side of the stem
   96 beats: 24 bars in 6 systems
  [ok]   a long melody breaks into systems, and every bar is drawn once
  [ok]   and every system but the last is justified to the same right edge
  [ok]   two instruments are two staves, each with its own clef

-- Scene 5: the metre --
  [ok]   in 6/8 six eighths are beamed in TWO threes -- by the dotted quarter, not the quarter
  [ok]   and a metre that is not one is refused

-- Scene 6: what the staff cannot show is COUNTED --
  [ok]   drum strokes are drawn on a percussion staff of their own, and nothing is lost
  [ok]   slendro, which no staff can write, is drawn at the nearest quarter tone and counted
  [ok]   the page is well-formed SVG (52 elements), with a treble clef in it

