 jins rast: 0 to 500 cents

  [ok]   Dhil's rungs are its declared degrees, the octave included: 0 200 350 500 700 900 1050 1200
  [ok]   and its steps are the tone, the three-quarter tones and the tone again, adding to the octave
  [ok]   the half-flat third is 350 cents: half way between a minor third (300) and a major one (400)
  [ok]   each step is named in tones where it is one: 150 is a three-quarter tone
  [ok]   the jins below the tonic spans -500 to 0 cents (rast on G), the one above 0 to 500
  [ok]   the sources' variants of the third (300, 400) are drawn as their own dotted rungs
  [ok]   a jins counted from its own degree lands there: Sika's rast on its third spans 350 to 850
  [ok]   Rast's seventh is 1050 going up and 1000 coming down: the descending form is its own rung
  [ok]   slendro's octave is 1208 cents, as measured -- not forced to 1200 -- and its 231-cent step has no tone name
  [ok]   the ladder keeps the tonic the universe was given: Rast on D starts at 293.66 Hz
